(7787592, 1296255, 36065, '<td valign="top">
<b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b>
<br/>
<br/><b>My thoughts on the image:</b> Those little jokers can be hard to catch for photos!  I remember stalking on for about 2 hours the first time I saw one in Glacier.  He was hiding in the parking lot, dipping in and out from underneath cars.  Nice capture and nice job meeting the challenge!
<br/>
<br/><b>My ideas for improvement: </b> This is a fantastic image, and I think it scored decently.  It seems like the voters are more often drawn to vibrant colors over interesting subjects.  I brown animal on a brown background probably didn''t translate well for many, especially if they don''t know how difficult they are to catch a good image of.
<br/>
<br/><b>Where I would have/did score this entry:</b> I did vote in this one, and I was one of your 6s.  I was between a 6 and 7, but leaned 6 based on comparison with the rest of the field.  Nice capture, and thanks for sharing!
<br/>
<br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,
<br/><b>Eric</b>
<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club

